"""Render concise lead reports for the fixed batch02 queue from inspected artifacts."""
import csv, json
from pathlib import Path

B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
NOTES={
'158965683':('REFUTED','complete','The s80 flagged dip at BTJD 3506.014 is the end of a monotonic ~25 ppt ramp and lies at the sector endpoint; the s80 brightening at 3491.139 is a broad ~42 ppt hump. The earlier s40/s53/s79 raw sectors show no comparable event. These are positive non-eclipse morphology, with the local side-window statistic distorted by the ramp.','No secure eclipse ephemeris. If astrophysical variability is of interest, obtain an independently extracted light curve and inspect the broad hump.','No isolated eclipse center; no physical period or depth reported.'),
'54494046':('PROBABLE','COMPLETE','Raw s45 BTJD 2527.768 and s72 BTJD 3264.431 show deep, smooth, roughly 2-day troughs. The s43 ending near 2498 and s71 beginning near 3235 show partial analogous troughs. Across three flux thresholds, s43 ingress to s72 ingress spans 13 cycles at 58.926–58.931 d, while s45 egress to s71 egress spans 12 cycles at 58.928–58.929 d. Adjacent integer aliases give incompatible clocks (about 54.4–54.7 or 63.8–64.3 d); thus four independent occasions support two alternating eclipse kinds. The two full minima alone are opposite kinds and cannot set the clock. The s72 TESSCut alternate extraction retains the broad trough (42.5 ppt core-to-side statistic, biased low by in-event side baseline) and difference centroid lies 0.067 pixel from target, but two Gaia neighbors at 12.67 and 18.00 arcsec are capable under approximate G-band bounds; attribution remains unresolved.','Resolve capable neighbors with multi-aperture/difference-image modeling and measure an additional complete same-kind eclipse.','Contact threshold alias diagnostics in partial-contact-aliases.json are not a formal ephemeris; Gaussian descriptive minima and QLP SAP depth in measured-events.json; no secure period error or primary epoch.'),
'231694897':('PLAUSIBLE','COMPLETE','The one s94 candidate near BTJD 3875.114 is a shallow ~5 ppt asymmetric depression followed by a ~1-day gap and different post-gap baseline. Seven cached QLP sectors show no comparable secure event. The live MAST TESSCut inventory adds s1, s103 and s105. s105 has measurable target flux and quality-zero cadence at conditional BTJD 4222.924 (s94 event plus six Gaia periods) without a comparable dip, though a slow local slope and the unmeasured s94 center limit that null. s103 cutout has only near-zero net target counts, so its central coverage cannot be counted as a null; s1 cutout returned no usable FFIs. These additional outcomes do not positively refute a one-off eclipse.','Obtain an independent s94 pixel extraction and a new raw observing occasion if the source remains of interest.','Single insecure event; no period, epoch, or depth fit. Missing-sector receipts and local-background TESSCut measurements in missing-cutout-review.json; s103/s1 unusable.'),
'396696012':('REFUTED','complete','All eight raw sectors show repeated smooth waves with characteristic spacing of several days, including alternating bright crests and broad troughs. The s31/s97/s98 flagged dips are pieces of this changing waveform; the s97/s98 recurrence does not identify a 37.32-day eclipse kind. Full-sector context provides positive evidence for quasi-periodic non-eclipse variability.','Characterize the shorter-period variability separately if desired; do not infer an eclipse period from these screening windows.','No eclipse period, epoch, or depth.'),
'278388101':('REFUTED','complete','The s80 flagged dip at 3492.604 is an asymmetric broad descent into a flat low state near an internal gap; the flagged brightening at 3504.320 is an irregular broad hump. s26/s40/s53/s54 do not show a matching shape. The raw profile supplies positive evidence for slow variability or reduction artifacts rather than an isolated eclipse.','If pursuing the variable, compare custom pixel extraction across the s80 state changes.','No eclipse ephemeris.'),
'467963921':('PROBABLE','complete','Three clean narrow raw SAP dips occur in s66, s94 and s103 at BTJD 3119.898, 3865.640 and 4163.932. The 15- and 6-cycle spacings each give about 49.716 d; quality-zero coverage excludes a 24.858-day half-period alias at s67, s93 and s104. Independent TESSCut extraction of s94 retains ~13.5 ppt depth; its difference centroid is 0.094 pixel from the WCS target. The brightest listed Gaia neighbor in 60 arcsec is far too faint under an approximate G/full-inclusion disappearance bound. Simple Gaia conjunction predictions are 4–5 days later; covariance-aware orbital compatibility has not been established.','Resolve Gaia phase/covariance and test other plausible orbital geometry; retain the measured eclipse period separate from Gaia P.','Descriptive raw Gaussian centers and depths in measured-events.json; no formal timing error.'),
'303916910':('REFUTED','complete','The only flagged s101 dip at 4112.908 is a monotonic descent cut off by a multi-day gap and followed by a shifted baseline. Eight other raw sectors do not show an analogous isolated trough. The plot supports a gap/baseline artifact interpretation for this screening window.','No eclipse follow-up warranted from this event alone; reassess if a new independent occasion appears.','No eclipse ephemeris.'),
'71469729':('REFUTED','complete','The s6 flags around 1483.8 and 1486.5 are embedded in irregular broad fluctuations; the s98 4010.061 dip is an abrupt discontinuity at a gap with sloping shoulders. s87 and s98 also contain bright humps with no stable eclipse profile. The repeated screening labels mix different physical shapes and do not establish same-kind recurrence.','Inspect the irregular variability as a separate source if of interest; seek independent raw events before an eclipse claim.','No eclipse period, epoch, or depth.'),
'323818250':('PLAUSIBLE','COMPLETE','Two weak s11 flagged windows near 1600.4 and 1603.95 are only ~2 ppt and blend into a slowly varying baseline; 30-min cadence and sparse samples limit morphology. Seven other cached QLP sectors supply no comparable secure event, while some predicted windows touch sector boundaries. The live MAST inventory adds s10 and s65; both TESSCut pixel cubes have near-zero local-background net target counts despite WCS placement, so they provide no valid photometric null. There is no positive artifact demonstration that refutes the insecure event.','If additional photometry becomes available, verify the s11 shape through an alternate extraction and target pixel attribution.','No measured eclipse period, epoch, or depth. Missing-sector receipts and unusable local-background TESSCut diagnostics in missing-cutout-review.json.'),
'233082910':('REFUTED','complete','Forty raw sectors contain a persistent smooth short-timescale oscillation, with repeated crests and troughs every few days. The many bulk dip and brightening flags select extrema of this oscillation and sector trends; they do not form a 52.66-day eclipse train. This is positive evidence for non-eclipse variability.','Study the short-period oscillation separately if desired; suppress its harmonics before any new long-period eclipse search.','No eclipse ephemeris from this screen.'),
}
rows=list(csv.DictReader((B/'queue.csv').open(newline='',encoding='utf-8')))
results=[]
for r in rows:
    tic=r['tic']; verdict,completion,assessment,next_check,limits=NOTES[tic]
    completion=completion.upper()
    src=json.loads((B.parent/'source-packets'/tic/'sources.json').read_text())
    text=f'''# {r['sample_id']} — TIC {tic}\n\n**Physical verdict:** {verdict}. **Bounded review:** {completion}. **Novelty:** UNKNOWN; four shared VizieR gates were unqueried after a positive-control timeout.\n\nSelected as `{r['sample_stratum']}` from the sealed queue. Gaia DR3 source {r['gaia_dr3']} has a spectroscopic period {r['gaia_period_days']} d; that is a selection orbit, not an eclipse period.\n\n{assessment}\n\n**Limitations:** {limits} The full available cached raw SAP sectors and representative flagged windows are documented in [raw-inspection.json](raw-inspection.json) and [orbit-context.json](orbit-context.json). The panel centers are screening predictions, not measured eclipse times. The [source packet](../../source-packets/{tic}/sources.json) records Gaia metadata and FITS hashes; `inspect_raw.py` independently checked every used FITS hash.\n\n**Next check:** {next_check}\n'''
    (B/tic/'REPORT.md').write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
    measured={'467963921':('49.7160','','','15.0'),
              '54494046':('58.93','','','')}.get(tic,('','','',''))
    results.append({'sample_id':r['sample_id'],'tic':tic,'sample_stratum':r['sample_stratum'],
                    'physical_verdict':verdict,'full_review_completion':completion,
                    'novelty_status':'UNKNOWN','period_days':measured[0],
                    'period_error_days':measured[1],'primary_epoch_btjd':measured[2],
                    'depth_ppt':measured[3],'limitations':limits,'next_check':next_check,
                    'report':str((B/tic/'REPORT.md').resolve())})
    print(r['sample_id'],tic,verdict,completion)
with (B/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8') as f:
    writer=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(results[0]));writer.writeheader();writer.writerows(results)
